From: Haocheng Yu <l1za0.sec@gmail.com>

Hi,

We found a kernel BUG in ocfs2_recover_node() while fuzzing Linux with a
modified version of syzkaller. We couldn't find a report of the same issue =
on
syzbot. We are investigating the root cause and trying to develop a fix. Co=
uld
you let us know whether this issue warrants a fix?

The crash occurs on Linux v7.3.0-rc5. The kernel hits the BUG at=20
fs/ocfs2/journal.c:1838 from the OCFS2 recovery thread and terminates with =
an=20
invalid-opcode Oops.

Relevant stack trace:

  ocfs2_recover_node (fs/ocfs2/journal.c:1838)
  __ocfs2_recovery_thread (fs/ocfs2/journal.c:1547)
  kthread (kernel/kthread.c:436)
  ret_from_fork (arch/x86/kernel/process.c:158)
  ret_from_fork_asm (arch/x86/entry/entry_64.S:245)

The reproducer mounts a crafted OCFS2 image with the nouser_xattr,
heartbeat=3Dnone, and commit mount options. The crash then occurs asynchron=
ously
in the OCFS2 recovery thread.

